  "question": {
    "text": "If one of the diameters of the circle, given by the equation, <math><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></math> is a chord of a circle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math>, whose centre is at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, then the radius of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math> is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>5</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>10</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>5</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>5</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The centre of the given circle <math><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and the radius is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>.</p><p>​​​​​​​<img src=\"assets\\st0138_b1a8a0f61a92.png\" style=\"width: 220px; height: 139px;\" /></p><p>The distance between the centres <math><mn>5</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math> and radius is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>. The triangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> is a right angled triangle<br /><br /><math><mi>O</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><msqrt><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><msqrt><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math><br /><br />Hence answer is <math><mn>5</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math></p>"
  }
}